# Mutation plan for the three channel-creation routes.
#
#   MUTATE_STORE_TARGETS='--test db_channel_creates' \
#     scripts/mutate-batch.sh scripts/mutations/channel-creates.plan
#
# `MUTATE_STORE_TARGETS` narrows the `store` lines to the one binary that covers them; without it
# `--tests` builds every mm-store test binary per mutation and lets an unrelated one decide the
# verdict.
#
# The decisions worth mutating here are the ones a reader would get backwards:
#
#   * the creator's `scheme_admin: true`, which no create response can show;
#   * the `PublicChannels` upsert, which decides whether a new channel is findable at all;
#   * the two *different* per-team counts, one in the store and one in the app layer;
#   * the conflict lookup's missing `DeleteAt` filter, which is why an archived channel keeps
#     its name;
#   * the self-DM's single membership row;
#   * which of `userIds[0]` and the session's user becomes `direct_added`'s `creator_id`;
#   * the addressing of all three events — user, channel, per-member — where getting it wrong
#     leaks a channel's existence or delivers to nobody.
#
# The last two lines are the no-op controls and must SURVIVE.
save-skips-the-public-channels-upsert	crates/mm-store/src/channel_store.rs	    upsert_public_channel(&mut tx, channel).await?;\n\n    tx.commit().await.map_err(|source| StoreError::Db {\n        context: "commit_transaction".to_owned(),\n        source,\n    })?;\n\n    Ok(ChannelSave::Saved)	    let _ = &channel;\n\n    tx.commit().await.map_err(|source| StoreError::Db {\n        context: "commit_transaction".to_owned(),\n        source,\n    })?;\n\n    Ok(ChannelSave::Saved)	store	save_propagates_a_public_channel
